      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "V655O",
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For a&nbsp;closed organ pipe, the resonate frequency(harmonics) is an odd multiple of the&nbsp;fundamental frequency.</p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>20000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>,&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kHz</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;fundamental frequency</p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>The total number of overtones&nbsp;that can be heard&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>.&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;harmonic to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>7</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;harmonic. )</p></blockquote>",
